Subject: [PATCH] ffmpeg: wait for a whole ALAC packet before decoding

The ffmpeg decoder is called once streambuf holds READ_SIZE (16 KB), on the
assumption that this always gives ffmpeg enough new data. An ALAC packet
holds 4096 frames and can be larger: about 24.6 KB for stereo 24 bit
uncompressed, up to 32 KB for 32 bit. When the stream fills streambuf more
slowly than the decoder drains it (high sample rates, slow network), the
mov demuxer asks for the rest of the packet while streambuf is momentarily
empty: _read_data returns 0, ffmpeg takes it as end of file, logs
"Packet corrupt" and drops the truncated packet. 4096 frames of audio are
lost and the output is no longer bit-identical to the source.

Register the alc codec with a minimum read of the largest stereo ALAC
packet plus READ_SIZE (about 48 KB), so decode is only called with a whole
packet buffered. Each decode call reads one packet, so no more is needed: a
larger minimum holds back more of the stream, and on a short track the
decoder then waits for the end of the stream while the output runs dry (128
KB is 0.74 s at 44.1 kHz/16 bit and left a gap of silence). At the end of
the stream decode still runs on whatever is left (toend in decode.c). wma is
unchanged.

Source: ralph-irving/squeezelite 72e1fd8abfa9b2f8e9636f033247526920878718
Upstream: Not submitted

--- a/ffmpeg.c
+++ b/ffmpeg.c
@@ -28,6 +28,13 @@
 
 #define READ_SIZE  4096 * 4   // this is large enough to ensure ffmpeg always gets new data when decode is called
 #define WRITE_SIZE 256 * 1024 // FIXME - make smaller, but still to absorb max wma output
+// A whole ALAC packet must be in streambuf before decode is called: packets
+// (4096 frames) can be larger than READ_SIZE, up to 4096 * 2 ch * 4 bytes plus
+// a few header bytes for stereo 32 bit. With less buffered, _read_data returns
+// 0 on a momentarily empty streambuf, ffmpeg takes it as end of file and drops
+// the truncated packet ("Packet corrupt"): 4096 frames of audio are lost.
+// No more than that: what is held back here can underrun a short track.
+#define ALAC_MIN_READ (4096 * 2 * 4 + 64 + READ_SIZE)
 
 // FIXME - do we need to align these params as per ffmpeg on i386? 
 #define attribute_align_arg
@@ -783,7 +790,7 @@
 		static struct codec ret = { 
 			'l',         // id
 			"alc",       // types
-			READ_SIZE,   // min read
+			ALAC_MIN_READ, // min read
 			WRITE_SIZE,  // min space
 			ff_open_alac,// open
 			ff_close,    // close
